{% set local_problem %}
<p>Athens' abundant tree coverage means gutters fill up fast. The historic neighborhoods around Athens Square and the university feature large, mature trees that drop leaves, seeds, and twigs constantly. Even newer subdivisions have enough tree coverage to keep gutters filling throughout the year.</p>

<p>The consequences of neglected gutters go beyond appearance. When gutters clog during Athens' heavy storms (55+ inches of rain annually), water overflows and cascades toward your foundation. Limestone County's soil conditions mean this water often pools rather than draining away, eventually finding its way into basements and crawlspaces.</p>

<p>Many Athens homeowners try to clean gutters themselves, but it's time-consuming, uncomfortable, and potentially dangerous work — especially on the historic multi-story homes found throughout the older parts of town. Professional cleaning is faster, safer, and more thorough.</p>

<p>Regular gutter cleaning is one of the most cost-effective ways to protect your Athens home from water damage.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our gutter cleaning service is comprehensive. We start by hand-removing all debris from inside your gutters — leaves, pine needles, roof grit, decomposed organic matter, and anything else that's accumulated. We don't just blow debris onto your lawn or push it toward the downspouts.</p>

<p>Next, we flush all downspouts with water to ensure they're clear and flowing properly. Downspout clogs are a common problem that many homeowners miss — debris backs up in the downspout, and the gutter overflows even though it looks clean from above.</p>

<p>Finally, we inspect your entire gutter system: hangers, seams, slope, and the fascia boards behind. We'll flag developing problems before they become expensive repairs. When we're done, we clean up all debris from your landscaping.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been cleaning gutters throughout Athens and Limestone County for over 20 years. From historic homes around the Square to newer construction, we've handled every gutter configuration and debris challenge this area presents.</p>

<p>Based just 22 miles away in Huntsville, we're close enough to respond quickly and local enough to care about doing the job right. When you call Blue River Gutters, you're talking to people who know Athens.</p>
{% endset %}
